fc"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-21","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":21,"english":"O exalted one, these feathered shafts of exceeding energy, sprung from the Kārtikeya forest, decked with gold, furnished with the plumes of the Kanka, resembling the thunderbolt of the great Indra, having smooth knots, and sharp heads, are like enraged serpents.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.8,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008021","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b86becada8573ac02dab15dd5158aeddffdbd60539cec502aedbee7ae3eb0186","compact":"c9731a1714ce14cb4a3d68b2e8e1a5114f8c21ad159911be6dc66219cb3e556a","nasal":"c9731a1714ce14cb4a3d68b2e8e1a5114f8c21ad159911be6dc66219cb3e556a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-22","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":22,"english":"O exalted one, these feathered shafts of exceeding energy, sprung from the Kārtikeya forest, decked with gold, furnished with the plumes of the Kanka, resembling the thunderbolt of the great Indra, having smooth knots, and sharp heads, are like enraged serpents.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008022","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f04d1429dbf0c0ad2c180e46f11f9b76103cebb7ed61d4f0e77ad623b44cb799","compact":"5d467d17a81833a31735dadd18e3f966d23f6db52e7b4f7966830017df07e9e5","nasal":"e832b602a336b08fe6b4ea9c885aee961abbc37f1db000fba703e07b11138a3c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-23","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":23,"english":"You shall behold your brother and enemy, who is named Vāli slain by my shafts, and lying like a dislodged hill.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.594,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008023","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2de28edf634bb19c25bf8a17b8975da27a565dbfa8270576a801f7eb236977a1","compact":"03d85eaea3d10bcf450c7a7accf240559e7feb7d29968340f551d7e2f6a73824","nasal":"03d85eaea3d10bcf450c7a7accf240559e7feb7d29968340f551d7e2f6a73824"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-24","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":24,"english":"Hearing Rāghava's words, Sugrīva-lord of host-felt excess of joy and exclaimed, Excellent well! Excellent well!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008024","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a43821079c28ab3e14cde6b3e3a5bd6af5a055ba8cdd752d2e495fb3d6ef3ee5","compact":"c643032c79b02a91c643049551b9f24c630471250a4eaf173c9a3af54f385300","nasal":"c643032c79b02a91c643049551b9f24c630471250a4eaf173c9a3af54f385300"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-25","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":25,"english":"O Rāma, overwhelmed am I by grief. You are the succour of those afflicted with sorrow. Having made you my friend, I express to you my grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008025","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b26b24c1900e1f815ceedf448265e285f1418eaf1c843a306e5ebfcf1aeea773","compact":"ea9fffefc6ae74920706d708d9445343be5be07d78dfbddd8351392a1cda04e5","nasal":"ea9fffefc6ae74920706d708d9445343be5be07d78dfbddd8351392a1cda04e5"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-26","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":26,"english":"I have, in the presence of Fire by giving you my hand, made you my friend. You are dearer to me than life itself. This I swear to you by Truth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.597,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008026","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2a9e8dadbad565934485194c500a4d060f3c9a27bfad69c9de014d2c496b6b5f","compact":"ec59d7a2974b2639835df05f609a1bfd51555428c7e27fa98d02ba771f4dd864","nasal":"ec59d7a2974b2639835df05f609a1bfd51555428c7e27fa98d02ba771f4dd864"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-27","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":27,"english":"Having made you my friend, I inspired with confidence am unbosoming myself to you. The sorrow, that is in my heart, is constantly enfeebling my mind.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.59,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008027","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0d905afcc3d315d8f2c23964e589948562c085b1fb44932a7edc92b3c31ea0f8","compact":"155568c3e2abf6dc2cc499a54eda1e59cf4ccaa2dd8f060db8498ad48204bd88","nasal":"10587b9d373cf404f5488afbbbefe50faa969d84beb0c688d3d4f8e14472409a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-28","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":28,"english":"Having proceeded thus far, he, his eyes filled with tears and his words faltering because of vapour, could not speak aloud.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.656,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008028","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e0e8919b2169031211a8c1036bce9f5c7eaeda1d2d9b96d077db84e359fb95df","compact":"b9e7d1ddffd38dbb4fc6fa15c420cc25189e7ca58ecdfdebf4f8410b78edb941","nasal":"b9e7d1ddffd38dbb4fc6fa15c420cc25189e7ca58ecdfdebf4f8410b78edb941"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-29","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":29,"english":"Sugrīva suddenly restrained, before Rāma, the force of tears, like to the tide of a river.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.981,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008029","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6429c328e8b514c983a48a4b90a252ea45405b003b1f9676b1ca9d9ca674b75b","compact":"2dcc628e5b830660e08513b485ab3fac8a6e14500077686abbee25c2d48b605f","nasal":"2dcc628e5b830660e08513b485ab3fac8a6e14500077686abbee25c2d48b605f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-30","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":30,"english":"Having restrained his tears and wiped his fair eyes, that energetic one, sighing heavily, again went on,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008030","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5d100daf68ba410332edc0f2aa94011bae83b07dbaea63bbfda13cccc9948dc7","compact":"3db52800cbfb23c80d51192de19451cddee8ecf8afd685c448cfee56a2c3c5f9","nasal":"3db52800cbfb23c80d51192de19451cddee8ecf8afd685c448cfee56a2c3c5f9"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-31","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":31,"english":"Formerly, O Rāma, I was deprived of my kingdom and reproached in harsh language by the strong Vāli.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008031","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"91fed722c1e0ea08cad7e91ac34cf7a173449b831d558be9509addcfd85c349a","compact":"0514e983765b47e41ab856ff2c22610c03c716d4d540f7892e9a526e0737869b","nasal":"0514e983765b47e41ab856ff2c22610c03c716d4d540f7892e9a526e0737869b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-32","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":32,"english":"He also took away my wife dearer to me than life; and my friends have been imprisoned and been bound.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.895,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008032","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"29534d550d8dad3035a85974766a99db829af739b6e1bf83a1e90198e7ff9c11","compact":"ce1abf20a9c8353b9db1714beff51434f1671c4dd4697fc87808c12b7c5397e2","nasal":"7baf197e5c185ecc1d05a3d01a275562d56f996de29ff9c0020d207529e2f59e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-33","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":33,"english":"That wicked wight, O Rāghava, seeks my life. Many monkeys commissioned by him have been slain by me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008033","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"90ca66c63b65c635286fd7e21cf687775698e185a0c73a54aaf6e3390470aeca","compact":"d51b72764f6061ab6af55e8d040d0a981738e1030d92c44184d91588913f4f94","nasal":"d51b72764f6061ab6af55e8d040d0a981738e1030d92c44184d91588913f4f94"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-34","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":34,"english":"It was, O Rāghava, in consequence of this fear that when I (first) saw you, I did not come out. This is all the fear that oppresses me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.825,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008034","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"16346e2a8e69b432cee83ef0eee91cdbac03f6a8629ee8273153133da5fa9b4e","compact":"e12188c5eef1d84b7633b48cb0db86361dd159b660db9f118b01a96fa7e180f2","nasal":"804706c18fb2da3dd6e786a8cd172a536c900138abe19333cbbf42e49e6b43e5"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-35","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":35,"english":"My adherents are only these headed by Hanumān. It is for this that although reduced to the greatest straits I have been able to preserve my life.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.866,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008035","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"12bdbdb2227f87e6327b6f282bad299096b1c92324a5f1ae76cbd37bd9090080","compact":"db1815d9e6fdb92d0d8be63b76080d26120f385dd9f19639b49415a98fdde2ee","nasal":"db1815d9e6fdb92d0d8be63b76080d26120f385dd9f19639b49415a98fdde2ee"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-36","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":36,"english":"These affectionate apes protect me on all sides. They go when I go, and stay when I stay.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.912,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008036","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ad79d6ad6bcb0db5cd189367f146c11838397a071f7444a08f666d2beb3ee3db","compact":"71568eb0450b2152143714d7bc9fa85e85a49abeca04c4b0f288d31f11ca94fc","nasal":"7ed6ff9434c35b59780e69f4294c791e08bac5d6b4e1a6e086683fac2629f3e4"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-37","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":37,"english":"Why should I expatiate? In brief, Vāli my elder brother, famed for his prowess, is my foe.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.822,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008037","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6d8949096837bc55fa8568883e66bdc098b39fadc7115ca5724276f4f7d52bb5","compact":"3f13b95ba14dd94a99038bbaf87a424a2b91a567614f68561fa9c365a6bd0875","nasal":"3f13b95ba14dd94a99038bbaf87a424a2b91a567614f68561fa9c365a6bd0875"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-38","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":38,"english":"Even by his death my present pain would be removed. Both my life and my happiness are bound up with his death.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.646,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008038","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e9e7c26f1310fa50f1097c52a70cfc619711ef8e6b1388f8b10471b2e8a99864","compact":"be7fa2d5a5069d763ac8ba35e9960b6279ede3c24c9e5528b049f342d0ab9eda","nasal":"8af13ea64566158d8be759c88f1bd3d679b0bbe2c27067576aa860f60e63094f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-39","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":39,"english":"I have, O Rāma, communicated to you, the way in which my grief might be removed. Whether in joy or in sorrow, a friend is the refuge of his friend.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.587,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008039","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"675a7f7eada4ff14343354c619d1730c7b408565bbbf6c3aca89c2266adf3ebf","compact":"1a98327fba2d2016903aedbaaca38cf04c54cd4e791e4bf380eb0baa965482ee","nasal":"2b4f7558613de25091fd667936a1fc926a43b36e073be9fd33c66dd8dfdf5385"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-40","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":40,"english":"Hearing these words, Rāma said to Sugrīva, What for arose hostility between yourself and Vāli? I wish to hear this (related) faithfully.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008040","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"afca944e1a318d0df1fd06ff8a10a8a2c811cff9c14fcee7eb8aa428de58bdb5","compact":"6dfb3d1783b7b743214c1bd950d22e80537465da8a245adfcf421c383e07204b","nasal":"6dfb3d1783b7b743214c1bd950d22e80537465da8a245adfcf421c383e07204b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-41","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":41,"english":"Having learnt the cause of your hostility, and ascertained your strength and weakness, I will, O monkey, understanding the irritation that has ensued, compass your happiness.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.733,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008041","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e5508e2f2efd497a9076a5e5bbbcd164acb3971a084fca1b2452787f67a06d90","compact":"ca017420758fdc90a4d6b542c797ebde5edc1fddbb1350cc6a2aa58d7dff7efc","nasal":"ac9896b5a3e35ab2019df3b94e6546c05de517ea731a2d5a59abfdd322a73634"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-42","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":42,"english":"Great is my wrath, on hearing you disgraced; and like a down-pour in the rainy season my ire increases, shaking my very heart.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008042","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e1d6b2ae73b9ec895b1bb1f56e38a64541f20f7117b560cdc682479ec0c5324","compact":"b0c824243df4776a64e49b326af5a43e24452ba889591a779e0cdbc21736fb9f","nasal":"776922cddfa1191d931e9412cc42a4f08206afd10cd26769c4291ae550d9402f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-43","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":43,"english":"Do you cheerfully and confidingly speak while I fix the string to my bow. As soon as my shaft is off, your foe is beaten.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-42"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008043","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"46e92d9613faabb71d9167047fbdf0501c4ce492ccfeeda62be77b89b7ae0503","compact":"bbc438e89ee62d3de9f2580fb29a535fca10fb02f5e8f8be34f87cc34aeadd7b","nasal":"bbc438e89ee62d3de9f2580fb29a535fca10fb02f5e8f8be34f87cc34aeadd7b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-44","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":44,"english":"Thus addressed by the high-souled Käkutstha, Sugrīva, along with the four (other) monkeys, experienced exceeding delight. Thus addressed by the high-souled Käkutstha, Sugrīva, along with the four (other) monkeys, experienced exceeding delight.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-43","DUTT-4-8-45"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008044","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"20ce96ac0f68dcd2a0a511ec7728a1bc4ca6102345a9b09fb274b0237f6f7a25","compact":"076064b9a3edf7d74f928445c0aad353fde2462fb423e799aa79703e2bf4ef85","nasal":"076064b9a3edf7d74f928445c0aad353fde2462fb423e799aa79703e2bf4ef85"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-8-45","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":8,"verse":45,"english":"Then with a cheerful countenance, Sugrīva began to unfold to Lakşmaņa's elder brother the cause of their hostility. Then with a cheerful countenance, Sugrīva began to unfold to Lakşmaņa's elder brother the cause of their hostility.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-8-44","DUTT-4-8-46"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4008045","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"22ccb684a505ff38e67ae7c06cdc6213cd177a0847971039600ca341d9390a9e","compact":"d3eed6694f1cab0dff025a2c6171a3d7532397015df48633a5abf849c5307975","nasal":"d3eed6694f1cab0dff025a2c6171a3d7532397015df48633a5abf849c5307975"}}]
